From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:18:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 175/192] wifi: ath11k: nss: don't return with conf_mutex held
 in sta_state

357-ath11k-fix-clear-peer-keys-during-disassoc.patch moved
ath11k_clear_peer_keys() into the AUTH -> ASSOC branch of
ath11k_mac_op_sta_state() with an early "return ret" - while
ar->conf_mutex is held.

ath11k_clear_peer_keys() returns -ENOENT when the peer is missing. That
is reachable in ieee80211_reconfig_stations(), which replays NOTEXIST ->
NONE -> AUTH -> ASSOC with WARN_ON() and carries on after a failure: if
the peer create failed during a hw restart on a wedged radio, AUTH ->
ASSOC returns with conf_mutex locked and the next call on that radio
(ASSOC -> AUTHORIZED in the same loop) deadlocks the restart worker with
the wiphy lock held.

Keep the warning and the error code, but leave through the common
unlock.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index 4d73914..615aee1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10599,11 +10599,9 @@ static int ath11k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		 * IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED to IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC)
 		 */
 		ret = ath11k_clear_peer_keys(arvif, sta->addr);
-		if (ret) {
+		if (ret)
 			ath11k_warn(ar->ab, "failed to clear all peer keys for vdev %i: %d\n",
-					arvif->vdev_id, ret);
-			return ret;
-		}
+				    arvif->vdev_id, ret);
 	} else if (old_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC &&
 		   new_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED) {
 		spin_lock_bh(&ar->ab->base_lock);
